      "outputTokens": 959,
      "costUsd": 0.008695,
      "pronunciationText": "Last video ended on this question: if a curve has gradient two x at every x, which curve is it? Here's that rule on a plant stand. Three bean plants grow by the same rule. t weeks after they sprout, each tip rises at two t centimetres per week. So each tip's height has gradient two t at every moment. But they sit on different shelves, so their height graphs are the same shape, slid up. Now one fact: one tip is sixty-six centimetres above the floor after four weeks. Which shelf is it on? And how does a whole family of curves become one curve?"
    },
