      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 90,
      "outputTokens": 649,
      "costUsd": 0.005886,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the name for what we're finding. If a function, capital F, has derivative f, then capital F is called a primitive of f. So x squared is a primitive of two x, and each tip's height is a primitive of its growth rate. Finding a primitive runs differentiation backwards. Differentiating takes x squared to two x. Finding a primitive starts at two x and asks, what did this come from?"
    },
