      "costUsd": 0.009892999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Two more facts handle whole polynomials. The derivative of a sum is the sum of the derivatives. So if F is a primitive of f, and G is a primitive of g, then F plus G is a primitive of f plus g. And k times F is a primitive of k times f, for any constant k. Now the notation for the whole family. The integral of f of x, d x, equals F of x, plus C. The function inside is called the integrand, and d x says that x is the variable. This is called the indefinite integral, and finding it is called integration. So the integral of x to the n is x to the n plus one, over n plus one, plus C."
    },
