      "inputTokens": 136,
      "outputTokens": 1204,
      "costUsd": 0.010904,
      "pronunciationText": "Now a worked example. Find the integral of three x squared, plus four x, minus five, d x. Work term by term. Three x squared becomes three, times x cubed over three, which is x cubed. Four x is four x to the one, so it becomes four, times x squared over two, which is two x squared. Minus five is minus five x to the zero, so it becomes minus five x. Add one C for the whole answer, because the constants from each term combine into a single constant. Now check by differentiating back. The derivative is three x squared, plus four x, minus five. That's the integrand exactly."
    },
