      "pronunciationText": "Now the main idea in one problem. A curve has gradient d y by d x equals three x squared, minus four x, plus two, and it passes through the point one, five. Find its equation. Integrate first. y equals x cubed, minus two x squared, plus two x, plus C. That's a whole family, every member the same shape. The point picks one. Substitute x equals one, and y equals five. Five equals one, minus two, plus two, plus C, which is one plus C. So C is four. The curve is y equals x cubed, minus two x squared, plus two x, plus four. A fact like this, the value of the function at one x, is called an initial condition."
